Package: E3ExpressionShiny
Title: Grant-Focused Shiny Reporter for the ARIA Plant E3 Resource
Version: 0.18.0
Authors@R: c(
    person("Peter", "Thorpe", role = c("aut", "cre"), email = "p.thorpe@dundee.ac.uk")
    )
Description: A modular Shiny application for querying and visualising candidate
    discovery, OrthoFinder grouping, E3-domain, Expression Atlas, ligandability,
    pocket-conservation, three-dimensional alignment and provenance evidence.
    It reads a completed DuckDB, a single candidate-level master Parquet or all
    current-run Parquet results through lazy, bounded DuckDB and duckplyr
    queries. A separate threshold explorer re-evaluates documented candidate
    gates without changing the primary analysis or rerunning scientific stages.
    A glossary defines the computational language and thresholds. A linked
    visual explorer combines a multi-axis candidate landscape, exact supporting
    tables, expression heatmaps and species-by-tissue profiles without
    conflating unavailable evidence with measured zero.
    Dedicated human and plant-human root-level hierarchical-orthogroup views
    retain candidate ranking, identifier, co-member and available sequence
    context. A pasted-list search spans recognised identifiers and names while
    retaining source-relation and matched-field provenance.
    An independent structural-review shortlist returns 200 to 500 root-level
    groups from the recorded discovery, orthology/species, domain and expression
    evidence rank while excluding existing structural-stage results. A dedicated
    seed catalogue prefers exact known-seed authority rows, retains source-scope
    provenance and exports available accession-matched sequences. Every primary
    tab provides collapsed contextual operating help with an explicit account
    of what the tab yields. Scientific tabs also provide a separate collapsed
    methods-and-thresholds annotation with recorded production settings,
    interpretation boundaries and method references where applicable. The
    complete-results browser
    adds joined root-HOG overview and member-detail views with both ranking
    stages, separate human, Arabidopsis, rice and barley representatives,
    membership summaries, structural support and assessed-member druggability,
    plus all fields from the strongest available HOG-linked ranking relation
    while preserving raw relations for exact audit.
    Optional offline pocket-review pages provide interactive selected-group
    structure, pocket-location and pocket-annotated alignment views.
